{
  "_comment": [
    "Canonical condition taxonomy for the medication catalogue.",
    "",
    "`category` on a medication is a DRUG CLASS label ('NSAID', 'Diuretic',",
    "'Inhaled Corticosteroid') that grew organically and mixes classes with",
    "conditions ('Diabetes', 'Cystic Fibrosis'). It stays as-is because it",
    "drives display labels (medications.categories.* i18n keys), the related-",
    "medications rail and price-estimate defaults.",
    "",
    "`condition` answers the question patients actually ask -- what is this",
    "for -- and is a small closed set. It is derived from category by the map",
    "below, with per-medication overrides for the handful of drugs whose class",
    "does not imply their use here (nadolol is a beta blocker, but in this",
    "catalogue it prevents variceal bleeding in liver disease).",
    "",
    "Run `npm run conditions:apply` after editing to rewrite the resolved",
    "`condition` field on every record in medications.json. It exits non-zero",
    "if a category has no mapping, so a new category cannot ship unclassified."
  ],

