  "categoryAliases": {
    "_comment": [
      "Category names collapsed onto the one that survives. Two groups:",
      "",
      "1. Merged duplicates. These were exact synonyms, not clinical",
      "   distinctions: the site displayed 'Pain Relief' and 'Pain Management'",
      "   as two separate groups holding three opioids between them, and",
      "   sevelamer sat in both 'Kidney Support' (as Renvela) and 'Phosphate",
      "   Binder (ESRD)'.",
      "",
      "2. Database vocabulary. The medications table grew plural category",
      "   names ('Immunosuppressants') while every sentence and label on the",
      "   site was written for the singular ('Tacrolimus is an",
      "   immunosuppressant...'). scripts/sync-medications-json.js has always",
      "   translated these on read; migration 048 applies them to the rows so",
      "   both sides finally agree, and the read-time translation stays as a",
      "   safety net for rows added later.",
      "",
      "Applied to medications.json by scripts/apply-medication-conditions.js,",
      "to database rows by migration 048, and to future database reads by",
      "scripts/sync-medications-json.js."
    ],

    "Pain Relief": "Pain Management",
    "Anemia (ESRD)": "Anemia",
    "Phosphate Binder (ESRD)": "Kidney Support",
    "Asthma Biologic / Allergy": "Asthma Biologic",

